WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.909
Meet MFA, your verification codes right in your browser.

00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:06.558
Let us walk through your first account together.

00:00:07.553 --> 00:00:11.399
First, install MFA from the Chrome Web Store and pin it to your toolbar.

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:14.129
Click its icon to open your account list.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.335
First, turn on two-step verification on the website you want to protect, and save its QR code.

00:00:19.535 --> 00:00:25.099
In MFA, select Add Account, then Scan QR Code, and choose the image.

00:00:25.299 --> 00:00:28.276
Review the account details and select Save.

00:00:28.476 --> 00:00:32.112
You can also paste a QR image or link, or enter a secret manually.

00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:36.003
Each account card shows a code and the time remaining.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:42.350
On a sign-in page, open MFA and click the matching account to try filling the code.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.955
You can enable clipboard fallback in Settings if filling is not available.

00:00:46.953 --> 00:00:49.407
Drag account cards to change their order.

00:00:49.607 --> 00:00:54.810
Right-click an account to edit it, view its QR code, or download a QR image.

00:00:55.787 --> 00:00:59.326
Open Password protection in Settings. Set and confirm your master password.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:04.863
You can now lock your vault with the button at the top. Enter your password to unlock it again.

00:01:05.063 --> 00:01:06.619
Keep your master password somewhere safe.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:13.014
Finally, select Export in Settings. With password protection enabled, the default is an encrypted backup.

00:01:13.214 --> 00:01:17.972
On your next device, select Import, decrypt the file, review your accounts, and confirm.

00:01:18.953 --> 00:01:21.991
MFA. Your verification codes, right in your browser.

00:01:22.191 --> 00:01:24.418
Now you are ready to add your first account.